[en.FOCUS_C01_MILITARY_SUPPLY]
Supply Construction

[en.FOCUS_C01_MILITARY_SUPPLY_desc]
A war is not won by a single battle, not by the strength of a single army, not by the power of a single weapon or spell, but by the overall strength of a nation, by the industry and logistics that allow a nation to fight persistently. If every little pony on the front line can enjoy a fresh cupcake from the Canterlot Bakery, then we have already won half the war... Well... If we replace these cupcakes with ammunition, maybe we can win three quarters of the war. Let’s go with that.

[zh.FOCUS_C01_MILITARY_SUPPLY]
补给建设

[zh.FOCUS_C01_MILITARY_SUPPLY_desc]
战争比拼的不是一场战斗的输赢，不是一个军团的强弱，不是一种武器或魔法的威力，而是一个国家的综合实力，让一个国家能够持久作战的工业和后勤能力。让每只远在前线的小马，都能美美地品尝坎特洛特糕点店新鲜出炉的杯糕，那么这场战争，我们就已经赢了一半...嗯...把这些杯糕换成弹药，也许能赢四分之三。还是这么办吧。

